WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.340
- If watching "The Queen's Gambit"

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.020
has you looking to make
your next move in content,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.820
you're in luck because we have five picks

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.070
that are sure to be a checkmate
on this week's Binge Guide.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.230
The first season of "The
Queen's Gambit" has fans

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.980
and critics swooning over
its stylized storytelling

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.080
and compelling characters
that feel so real,

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.590
yet, stunningly, are all works of fiction.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.640
So, if you can't decide
what move to make next,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.670
we have put together
five titles that we think

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.590
are a part of a winning binge strategy,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.137
starting with our
actor's spotlight "Emma."

00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:29.450
"Queen's Gambit" star
Anya Taylor-Joy stars

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.970
in this British period
comedy-drama adaptation

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.310
of the Jane Austen novel of the same name

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.390
as Emma Woodhouse, a young
woman in 19th century England,

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.370
whose antics in matching
are simply delightful.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.140
Fans of Taylor-Joy will
love seeing her show off

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.030
her lighter side after darker roles,

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.650
like in "The Witch" or "Split."

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.770
And while it might not
stick to the exact tone,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.020
critics say Jane Austin
fan should still find

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.180
a solid match in "Emma"

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.150
and have praised it for
its modern approach,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.337
energy, and unique adaptation.

00:00:56.337 --> 00:00:59.130
"Emma" has a total run time
of two hours and five minutes,

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.790
which is basically a nice healthy break

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.140
between your marathon chess sessions.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.030
Next up is our throwback pick
and that's going to "Mad Men,"

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.030
which debuted back in 2007.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.850
This drama is about a high
profile ad agency in New York

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.220
in the 1960s, it's enigmatic
ad exec Don Draper,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.820
and tons of drinking.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.530
John Hamm picked up two
Golden Globes and an Emmy

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.650
for his breakout performance

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.590
playing said drinking executive Draper

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.030
across seven Certified Fresh seasons.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.500
But it's the '60s ambiance,
brilliantly crafted characters,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.960
and razor-sharp writing that
will have "Queen's" fans

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.570
feeling especially at home.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.290
It'll take you about 79 hours
to binge the whole series,

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.950
which is just enough time
to master all the cocktails

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.320
while soaking in all that
great mid-century design.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.700
Everything just seems so
much cooler back then.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.560
Moving on to our brand new pick this week

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.350
and it's going to "The Great."

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.230
Starring Elle Fanning and Nicholas Hoult,

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:51.200
this genre-bending comedy-drama
follows Catherine the Great

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.000
on her rise to power
in 18th century Russia.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.200
Now, the show features
delicious performances

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.500
and a wicked sense of humor,

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.000
and it was just renewed
for a second season,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.800
so there's even more greatness on the way,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.270
which is great for us.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.000
And with just 10 episodes
at just under an hour each,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.650
you can binge just one in
roughly eight and a half hours.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.550
And for our Certified
Fresh pick this week,

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.550
we are jumping all the
way back to the '50s

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.280
to "The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel."

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.840
Rachel Brosnahan stars
is Miriam 'Midge' Maisel,

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.130
a housewife who's
blissful life is uprooted

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.990
after she discovers her true
calling: standup comedy.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.360
This award-winning Amazon Prime series

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.820
from "Gilmore Girls" creator
Amy Sherman-Palladino

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.900
has been recognized for its
ability to deliver warmth,

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.230
empowerment, and a whole lot of laughs,

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.930
and its ensemble cast of characters

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.530
offers something for everyone.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.640
You can binge all three
seasons in just under 25 hours

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.900
and nobody will blame you if
you pick up some new jokes

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:41.750
along the way.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.810
And finally, our
family-friendly pick this week

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.840
is going to "Queen of Katwe."

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.060
This Certified Fresh feel good chess drama

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.100
snuck into theaters in 2016

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.350
and with "Queen's Gambit"
reigniting interest

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.330
in checkerboard action,

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.080
we think that is worth revisiting.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.250
Oscar winner Lupita
Nyong'o and David Oyelowo

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:01.480
star in this biographical
drama about Phiona Mutesi,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.780
a struggling slum-bound Ugandian girl

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.870
who learns to play chess and uses a game

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.180
and her exceptional
skill to propel herself

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.150
all the way to the World Chess Olympiad.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.980
Featuring uncommon smarts
and outstanding performances,

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:16.300
and with a total runtime of
just an hour and 24 minutes,

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.040
this one's a no-brainer for
people looking for a great film

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.410
on the shorter side or a
family-friendly alternative

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.090
to the more adult themes
on "Queen's Gambit."

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.630
All right, friends, well
hopefully this'll have you

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.910
saying checkmate on your
next few binge sessions.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.690
Be sure to let us know what
you are currently streaming

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:30.640
in the comment section.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.130
And don't forget to check back
here for more recommendations

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.860
based around the movies
and shows that you love

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.131
right here on the Rotten
Tomatoes Binge Guide.

00:03:37.131 --> 00:03:40.881
(upbeat instrumental music)

